Vertical blanks on time. The game thread paces each vertical blank with a timed wait on a condition variable, which on Windows ends on the system timer's tick (1 ms at best), so the frames shown on the vertical blanks came 14.5 to 18.9 ms apart instead of 16.68 (0.7 to 0.9 ms deviation in the city). Both timed waits of the scheduler now end 1.5 ms before the deadline and yield the rest away, checking for events: the gaps stay within about 15.8 to 17.6 ms (0.16 to 0.28 ms deviation), which matters on a variable refresh display, where each frame is shown when it is presented. PS2X_PRECISE_WAIT=0 keeps the plain wait.

